WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Good morning, Hank. It's Tuesday, but this video was filmed in the past.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.360
I mean, I guess that is always true but it more true than usual this time.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.140
I'm taking a week or two away from the internet to work,

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.300
so this video was actually filmed nine days ago.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.400
Has anything interesting happened in the last nine days?

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.680
Has a shocking scandal gripped the nation?

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:15.340
Probably.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.740
It seems like shocking scandals grip the nation every week,

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.120
and horrify and/or thrill us so much that we think,

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.940
"now this is a properly shocking scandal,"

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:26.060
and it is, until the next week when there is a new shocking scandal.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:29.800
As Dorothy Parker said a long, long time ago, "what fresh hell is this?"

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.860
But let us not talk of hells and freshness,

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.540
let's answer real questions from real nerdfighters, because it's Question Tuesday.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.060
What's in the boxes?!

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:39.620
Okay, absolutely true story. I recently opened one of the boxes,

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:41.700
and I was stunned to find what's inside.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:42.880
In fact, I'll just show you.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:46.200
So, we have here a box. I'm just gonna open it,

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.960
and, as you'll see, what's inside of this box...

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:52.780
... is another box.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:54.500
Do caterpillars know they'll turn into butterflies,

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.620
or while they're building the cocoon, are they just like, "what the heck am I doing?"

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:01.100
Well, we know that butterflies seem to be able to remember smells from when they were caterpillars,

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:04.200
although, admittedly, that's not quite the same thing as self-awareness,

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.440
but then again, do humans know what they are doing as they mature,

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.600
or are they just like, "what the heck am I doing?"

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:09.940
How do you cope with uncertainty?

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:14.020
Quite poorly. I desperately want to be able to close the loop on my thoughts,

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:19.240
like, I really want to be able to convince myself that something, really anything, is absolutely certain.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:23.760
On the other hand, I would argue that uncertainty is maybe a little under-appreciated in contemporary discourse,

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:27.960
like, it sometimes feels as if you're supposed to begin every conversation not only with a position,

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.880
but with absolute certainty that your position is correct,

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:35.700
and I personally find it difficult even to be certain about the proposition that I'm, like, an actual human being,

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:39.740
let alone what the top marginal income tax rate should be in the United States.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:41.100
What's your favorite word right now?

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.140
Non-sensorial.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:43.840
What are you looking forward to the most about Vid-Con?

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:45.480
I really love the annual Nerdfighter meet-up,

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:48.300
because we get to talk about future plans for Crash Course and other stuff.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:49.800
How's life post "100 Days"?

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:53.160
Good! I just finished my first half-marathon in a time of 2 hours and 7 minutes,

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:57.140
meaning that if I can just reduce my time by like an hour, I'll be a world class runner!

00:01:57.140 --> 00:01:59.220
I want to listen to the Mountain Goats, but where should I start?

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:01.780
Their new album just came out. It's called "Goths" and it's one of my favorites.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:05.860
It really took me back into my past with an intensity I haven't felt in a long time.

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:09.440
That said, I always recommend that you start with the album "All Hail West Texas".

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.480
My brother is expecting a baby soon. How can I prepare to be a great aunt?

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.320
Well, you're not actually going to be a great aunt, you're just going to be a regular aunt,

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:19.080
until, like, your brother's kid has a baby of its own, then you'll be a great—

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:22.180
No wait. You meant, like, "how can I prepare to be an excellent aunt?"

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:25.860
Don't worry about it. You're going to be great! Well, you'll be regular, but you know what I mean.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.280
What's your favorite pasta shape?

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.160
The bow-tie one.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:29.160
Favorite regular shape?

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:29.780
Spiral.

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:30.480
Favorite painting?

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.200
Probably this one by Raymond Pettibon.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.180
Favorite superhero?

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:36.380
Batman! No, I'm just kidding; Batman isn't a super hero. He is a rich person.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:39.140
My favorite comic-book super hero, at the moment, is probably Ms. Marvel.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:40.340
Favorite dog breed?

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.720
Mutts, although I am also partial to what Alice calls "Willy dogs"!

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:44.580
How is Willy?

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.340
Um, unfortunately, not great. Willy has cancer.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:50.380
It's a very slow growing kind of cancer, but it is cancer.

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:54.620
He's a great dog, and he's much loved, and we're hopeful he can have a good dog life for quite a while longer.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:56.120
So, I wanted to let you know that's going on,

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.760
but we're hopeful because he does have a relatively good prognosis.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.000
So, let's move on to happier news.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.980
What's going on with Russia and Trump?

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.640
I said, "happier news!"

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:08.380
How did AFC Wimbledon manage not to score a single goal in their final six games?

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.820
HAPPIER NEWS!!

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:12.480
Ashley Ford asks, "I just got engaged last night and I'm wondering,

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:15.200
"what's your best advice for a long and happy marriage?"

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:18.060
There we go! Some proper happy news! Congratulations!

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:23.340
The world goes on! People fall in love! Hope, "that thing with feathers," refuses to be shushed!

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:27.881
As to your question, I posted to Sara and she reminded me of this Philip Larkin poem that ends,

00:03:27.881 --> 00:03:29.740
"we should be careful of each other.

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:32.360
"We should be kind, while there is still time."

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:35.540
Hank, let us be careful of each other, and kind.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:36.620
I'll see you on Friday.

